<% if context_only? %>
  <%# Shown only as the path to a readable page below it (access-control
      design spec §3.3): greyed out, not a link, no status or actions. %>
  <div id="<%= dom_id %>" class="flex items-center gap-1.5 rounded-cs px-1.5 py-1">
    <span class="flex-1 truncate text-meta" title="<%= t(".context_only") %>"><%= title %></span>
  </div>
<% else %>
  <%# `relative`: the handle is placed against the row, outside its box. %>
  <div id="<%= dom_id %>" class="group/node relative flex items-center gap-1.5 rounded-cs px-1.5 py-1 hover:bg-sunken <%= row_class %>">
    <%# The homepage can't be moved (Pages::Move) -- no handle, nothing to
        grab; nor can a page the actor may not move, nor the top of a branch
        under a page they can't read. Every other node's
        handle is the only part of the row that starts a drag (admin--pages--tree's
        `handle:` option), so the title link below stays a plain, clickable
        link. %>
    <% if movable? %>
      <%# A real button, so the keyboard reaches it: Space picks the row up,
          the arrows move it, Space drops it (`admin--pages--tree#key`). The mouse
          drag still starts from it (SortableJS `handle:`).

          IN THE GUTTER, NOT IN THE ROW (Claude Design, 2026-10-13, T2): it
          stands in the 16px of indent to the row's left (`-left-4 w-4`,
          exactly the children list's `ml-2` + line + `pl-[7px]` below), so
          the title has the room it took. Every movable row has that gutter:
          only the homepage is not in a children list, and it has no handle.
          It is shown the way the hover control in a block card's header
          is (a control that is nothing at rest): by `opacity`,
          on hover of its row and while it has the focus, and always where
          ANY pointer of the device is coarse (`any-pointer-coarse:`, not
          `pointer-coarse:`, which asks about the first pointer only: on a
          touch-screen laptop that is the mouse, and the finger that cannot
          hover would never see the handle).
          `focus:` and not `focus-visible:`, because a row
          picked up with Space after a click on its handle must show what
          holds it. Not shown by `opacity` it is still there: in the Tab
          order, which is the keyboard's way to it, and under the pointer,
          so a press where it is starts the drag. Being a child of the row
          it keeps the row hovered while the pointer is on it, and it
          abuts the row, so the pointer crosses no gap on its way. Its
          chrome ground covers the guide line it stands on while it shows. %>
      <button type="button" class="admin-tree-node__handle absolute inset-y-0 -left-4 w-4 cursor-grab select-none rounded-cs bg-chrome text-center text-meta opacity-0 hover:text-ink focus:opacity-100 focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-accent group-hover/node:opacity-100 any-pointer-coarse:opacity-100"
              aria-label="<%= t(".move", title: title) %>" aria-describedby="tree-drag-help"
              data-action="keydown->admin--pages--tree#key focusout->admin--pages--tree#blur">⠿</button>
    <% end %>

    <%# `title:` is the full name for a row the narrow column truncates. %>
    <%= link_to title, path, id: link_id, title: title, data: { turbo_frame: "content" },
          aria: (selected? ? { current: "page" } : {}),
          class: "flex-1 truncate #{selected? ? "font-semibold text-ink" : "text-ink"}" %>

    <%# Draft, Scheduled or Live with changes, one small named mark (see the component). %>
    <%= render Admin::PagesScreen::TreeStateMarkComponent.new(page: page) %>

    <%# Outdated and missing translated fields (handoff §10 B24), summed over
        the target languages: plain text in a warn / meta ink, nothing at
        zero. `role="img"` + `aria-label` so a screen reader hears what the
        tooltip says; the glyph itself is decoration. HIDDEN AT REST by
        `sr-only` (`marker_class`), never `hidden` or `aria-hidden`, so the
        reader still hears them and they take no room until hover or focus. %>
    <% if translation_total(:outdated).positive? %>
      <%= tag.span "↻#{translation_total(:outdated)}", data: { translation_marker: "outdated" }, role: "img",
            title: translation_tooltip(:outdated), aria: { label: translation_label(:outdated) },
            class: "shrink-0 text-count text-warn-ink #{marker_class}" %>
    <% end %>
    <% if translation_total(:missing).positive? %>
      <%= tag.span "○#{translation_total(:missing)}", data: { translation_marker: "missing" }, role: "img",
            title: translation_tooltip(:missing), aria: { label: translation_label(:missing) },
            class: "shrink-0 text-count text-meta #{marker_class}" %>
    <% end %>

    <%# What features register at `tree.row.markers`, after the translation
        markers: each is told this row's page and its slice of what was
        loaded for the rows being drawn. %>
    <%= render Admin::Ui::SlotComponent.new(name: "tree.row.markers", record: page, viewer: Current.actor, loaded: loaded, locale: locale, url_options: url_options) %>

    <% if child_count.positive? %>
      <%# `role="img"` and a label, like the translation markers: a bare "3" says nothing.

          ON HOVER AND FOCUS ONLY (T2): the design shows the count on a
          collapsed row, where it says what is hidden, and on hover. The
          tree has no collapsing, so every row's children are in view below
          it and the count takes room from the title for nothing; it shows
          while the pointer is on the row or the focus is in it, and always
          where any pointer is coarse (as the handle). `sr-only` and not `hidden`, so a screen
          reader still reads "3 subpages" on a row at rest and the count
          takes no room there. When the tree learns to collapse, a
          collapsed row shows it at rest. %>
      <%= tag.span child_count, data: { child_count: true }, role: "img", aria: { label: child_count_label },
            title: child_count_label,
            class: "sr-only shrink-0 text-label text-meta group-hover/node:not-sr-only group-focus-within/node:not-sr-only any-pointer-coarse:not-sr-only" %>
    <% end %>

    <% if can_add_child? %>
      <%= link_to "+", new_child_path, data: dialog_trigger("new-page-dialog").merge("new-page-parent-id-param": page.id, turbo_frame: "content"),
            class: "shrink-0 rounded-cs px-1 text-meta opacity-0 hover:bg-surface hover:text-ink focus-visible:opacity-100 group-hover/node:opacity-100 pointer-coarse:opacity-100",
            aria: { label: t(".add_child", title: title) } %>
    <% end %>
  </div>
<% end %>
